### `tickets/003-append-log-merge-behavior.md`

```markdown
---
ticket: 003
title: Merge behavior of tracked machine-appended log files
type: research
status: open
blocked_by: []
claimed_by:
claimed_at:
---

## Question

How do tracked machine-appended log files actually behave under concurrent-branch
merges? Facts needed from outside this repo:

- `.gitattributes` `merge=union` driver semantics: line ordering, duplicate
  handling, and the cases where it silently does not apply (web-UI merges,
  rebase pulls, clones missing the attributes or hooks — both present on this
  team per map Notes).
- How GitHub/GitLab web merge UIs handle conflicts in union-merge-attributed files.
- Prior art that sidesteps append-conflicts entirely: changelog-fragment tools
  (towncrier, changesets, reno) using file-per-entry with a later assembly step.

## Resolution

<!-- findings land in assets/ + here; written by the research subagent pass -->
```

