## Question

Before any rule-ownership / review-gate design can even be judged, confirm whether
the host repo has — or can get — branch protection with required reviewers. This is
a platform setting no repo file can enforce.

Checklist (human or agent, read-only — no write window needed):
- [ ] Query current protection: `gh api repos/{owner}/{repo}/branches/{default}/protection`
- [ ] If absent: confirm the hosting plan allows it (e.g. GitHub private repos
      require a paid plan for required reviewers) and whether org policy permits
      enabling it.
- [ ] Record: available now / available after plan or org change / not available.

## Open Questions

- Should shared-doc changes require a review gate, and who owns the rules docs?
  Human unavailable for this during charting. **Conservative default (revisit):
  design assumes NO enforced review gate exists** — no decision may depend on
  branch protection until this ticket confirms availability; fallback is the
  convention-only, human-gated commit step already fixed in map Notes.

## Resolution

